  "id": "COMPOUND:23435 - PROTEIN:6324",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a complex but consistent pathway linking Eupomatenoid 5 to M-phase phosphoprotein 8 through multiple targets. Eupomatenoid 5 is identified as a target of several compounds, including Gypenoside Xlvi, Quercetagetin 3-methyl ether 7-glucoside, and 2-(2,6-Dihydroxyphenyl)-5-hydroxy-3,6,7-trimethoxychromen-4-one, all of which are known to target M-phase phosphoprotein 8. This indicates that Eupomatenoid 5 may act as a central mediator in the signaling cascade that leads to the activation of M-phase phosphoprotein 8. The high scores in the final scores suggest a strong, albeit indirect, relationship, likely mediated through the metabolic or signaling pathways of the compounds involved. The recurring involvement of SNU-387, a cell line that is a target of multiple compounds, further supports the idea that Eupomatenoid 5 is part of a broader network that influences the phosphorylation of M-phase phosphoprotein 8. The integration of these pathways highlights the potential role of Eupomatenoid 5 in modulating the cellular response to these compounds, possibly through a mechanism that involves the regulation of M-phase-related processes.",
